.TH CHMOD 1
.SH NAME
chmod \- change a file's permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chmod
.I mode path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chmod
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It sets the permissions of
.I path
to
.IR mode ,
an octal number: read 4, write 2, execute (or enter, for a directory) 1,
for the owner, the group and the others, as in
.B 644
or
.BR 755 ;
.B 1000
is the sticky bit (in a directory, only a file's owner may remove it).
Only the owner or root may change them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chmod 640 /tmp/grp.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chown (1),
.BR ls (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
Octal modes only (no
.BR u+x ),
one path at a time.
